think The research lap landed at ee093956c7. Repairing %440's eighth firing left one red standing
think and I did not want to accept the number without asking which guard. It was standing_equipment.
think The measurement is three points minutes apart, and it is direct rather than inferred. Cold
think pass 20260906.105803: index_row_bound red, honestly. I sorted the shelf. Hot pass
think 20260906.111808: index_row_bound GREEN at output line 60, standing_equipment RED at line 151
think -- later in the same pass. Then the same scan by hand two minutes after: runs_red=0, verdict=ok.
think Nothing changed between the last two but the run card being finished.
think The mechanism is in the card's own stamps: oldest_run equals newest_run across all 140 rows,
think one stamp, so the runner writes the card wholesale at the CLOSE of a pass. A guard reading it
think mid-pass therefore reads the PREVIOUS pass, whatever position it holds in the roster. Running
think it later cannot help; only writing incrementally, or running it after the write, can.
think Why this is not %475. That row closed the half where the guard counted its OWN verdict, and
think landed self_guard, red_self and runs_red_self. Here runs_red_self=1 is behaving correctly and
think runs_red counted a PEER's stale verdict. The mechanism %475 added cannot see this one, which
think is what makes it a separate row rather than a re-firing.
think The direction of the lag is the expensive one: it reports a fault already fixed, on the lap
think that fixed it. And the cost is priced already -- a red guard withholds roster_receipt_write,
think --scoped refuses without a full green receipt, so the next lap pays a full cold pass. Measured
think here at 900s cold and 687s hot.
obs Booked rather than repaired, and I said which two shapes fit: write the card incrementally, or
obs run that guard after the write. The runner and the roster are bakery's, and choosing between two
obs sound shapes in another seat's module is a ruling rather than a lap. Naming both is the whole of
obs what I can honestly hand over.
obs Fetch-before-book held: git fetch xy moved 05c87d3d0 to 2a3313c06 while my roster ran, and
obs --next answered 480 against the fetched spine rather than my local read. Booked, then
obs reds_spine_derive read squatters=0 double_booked=0 verdict=ok. The headline moved 479 to 480 and
obs reds_ledger_monotone went from headline_drift back to GREEN.
obs A small gap named, not fixed: tools/r/remember_git_nib.rish derives HEAD^ always, so it has no
obs mode for the follow-up case remember-git-nib rule 5 describes, where the nib must name HEAD read
obs before the commit is made. I wrote ee093956c7 by hand for that reason and record why here.
obs The card sat 534 bytes over its bound after this row went on. Rather than shave prose eight
obs times, I folded my landed half to where it actually lives -- the two errata, which hold the
obs account whole and are graded -- and kept the OPEN row whole on the card. That is the pin law's
obs own instruction and it should have been my first move rather than my fifth.
